.TH CLIP 1 "October 2026" "clip 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clip \- cross-platform command-line clipboard utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clip
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B clip
script reads data from standard input or specified file(s) and copies it to the system clipboard, or outputs current clipboard data when run in paste mode.
.PP
It automatically detects and adapts to the active graphical session, platform, or remote terminal, supporting:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Wayland
via \fBwl-copy\fR / \fBwl-paste\fR
.IP \(bu 2
.B X11
via \fBxclip\fR or \fBxsel\fR
.IP \(bu 2
.B Remote SSH / Headless
via \fBOSC 52\fR ANSI escape sequences
.IP \(bu 2
.B macOS
via \fBpbcopy\fR / \fBpbpaste\fR
.IP \(bu 2
.B WSL / Windows
via \fBclip.exe\fR / \fBpowershell.exe\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-o ", " \-\-paste
Paste current clipboard contents to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-clear
Clear current clipboard buffer immediately.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-trim
Trim trailing newline character from input data before copying.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-primary
Target the primary selection buffer instead of the standard clipboard (supported on X11, Wayland, and OSC 52).
.TP
.BR \-\-osc52
Force use of OSC 52 terminal ANSI escape sequence to copy data over SSH or inside tmux sessions.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Explicitly end option parsing; treat subsequent arguments as filenames even if they start with a dash.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Copy command output to clipboard:
.nf
$ date -I | clip
.fi
.TP
Copy file contents to clipboard:
.nf
$ clip myfile.txt
.fi
.TP
Copy multiple files (concatenated) to clipboard:
.nf
$ clip file1.txt file2.txt
.fi
.TP
Copy path without a trailing newline:
.nf
$ pwd | clip -n
.fi
.TP
Copy over remote SSH to local workstation clipboard:
.nf
$ cat /etc/os-release | clip --osc52
.fi
.TP
Clear the clipboard buffer:
.nf
$ clip -c
.fi
.TP
Paste clipboard contents to standard output:
.nf
$ clip -p
.fi
.TP
Save clipboard contents directly to a file:
.nf
$ clip -p > output.txt
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (e.g. no clipboard provider found, file not found, permission denied, or no input data provided).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wl-copy (1),
.BR wl-paste (1),
.BR xclip (1),
.BR xsel (1)
